# IOT workshop - MQTT and Home Assistant 

Welcome! In the workshop you will be learning how a Raspberry Pi Pico can be turned into an internet-connected smart home device.
Here is the list of components you need:
 - Inventor 2350W with Pico 2 W aboard 
 - BME280 pressure/temperature/humidity sensor
- Micro USB cable
 - University laptop
 - QW/ST cable
   
The workshop is broken down into exercises to be done in order. Please read everything carefully. If you need any help, let us know :D

|Exercise|
|-|
|[ 01 Setting up Thonny editor](../setting-up-thonny-editor/setting-up-thonny-editor.md)|
|[02 Flashing LEDs](02-flashing-leds/02-flashing-leds.md)|
|[ 03 Home Assistant](03-home-assistant/03-home-assistant.md)|

